\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\lang9 ForgeBot: Autonomous Cyber-Physical Robotics Factory\par
Meta Global AI Developer Hackathon \f1\emdash  "Push the Frontier" Track\par
\par
1. The Problem We Are Trying to Solve\par
Hardware prototyping, robotics design, and automation engineering are historically slow, highly fragmented, and bottlenecked by deep domain silos. If an engineer, researcher, or innovator wants to build a custom robotic system (e.g., a multi-axis inspection drone or a specialized delivery rover), they must manually navigate multiple disciplines:\par
\par
System Design & Component Selection: Sourcing compatible motors, microcontrollers, and chassis configurations while calculating payload and power limits.\par
\par
Mechanical Modeling & URDF Writing: Crafting intricate XML/CAD files (Unified Robot Description Format) with exact link dimensions, mass matrices, and joint constraints.\par
\par
Control Software & Firmware Engineering: Writing low-level C++/MicroPython or ROS2 nodes for motor control, sensor telemetry, and inverse kinematics.\par
\par
Validation Friction: Waiting weeks for physical parts to ship or complex desktop simulation environments (like heavy Gazebo/ROS setups) to configure just to see if a mechanism works.\par
\par
The Solution: ForgeBot bridges the gap between natural language intent and cyber-physical execution. It is an agentic, end-to-end robotics factory that ingests a plain-language objective and autonomously orchestrates the design, coding, simulation, and validation of a functional robotic system in seconds.\par
\par
2. Complete System Architecture\par
The architecture is built on a modular, high-performance stack separating cognitive reasoning, code generation, real-time spatial simulation, and visual processing.\par
